ojectGitStatus","target":"docs/Get-PSProjectGitStatus.md","line":40},{"title":"Open-PSProjectStatusHelp","target":"docs/Open-PSProjectStatusHelp.md","line":41},{"title":"New-PSProjectStatus","target":"docs/New-PSProjectStatus.md","line":211},{"title":"New PSProject Status","target":"images/new-psprojectstatus.png","line":213,"embedded":true},{"title":"new custom project status","target":"images/new-psprojectstatus2.png","line":222,"embedded":true},{"title":"Get-PSProjectStatus","target":"docs/Get-PSProjectStatus.md","line":253},{"title":"Set-PSProjectStatus","target":"docs/Set-PSProjectStatus.md","line":309},{"title":"remote repository status","target":"images/remote-repository.png","line":331,"embedded":true},{"title":"psproject methods","target":"images/psproject-methods.png","line":364,"embedded":true},{"title":"Get-PSProjectTask","target":"images/get-psprojecttask.png","line":399,"embedded":true},{"title":"New-PSProjectTask","target":"images/new-psprojecttask.png","line":405,"embedded":true},{"title":"list projects","target":"images/list-projects.png","line":424,"embedded":true},{"title":"project list","target":"images/manage-psproject.png","line":452,"embedded":true},{"title":"Get-PSProjectReport","target":"docs\\Get-PSProjectReport.md","line":456},{"title":"Sample verbose output","target":"images/verbose-output.png","line":645,"embedded":true},{"title":"1;38;5;77m\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n:heavy_exclamation_mark: You must use a PowerShell console that supports ANSI escape sequences. The PowerShell ISE __does not__ support this feature.\r\n\r\n## Editor Integration\r\n\r\nIf you import this module into your PowerShell editor, either Visual Studio Code or the PowerShell ISE, the module will add an update function called `Update-PSProjectStatus`. You can run the command from the integrated terminal or use the appropriate shortcut (see below). The command will the status based on user input, update the `LastUpdate` time to the current date and time, update the project version from the module manifest (if found), and update the git branch if found.\r\n\r\nYou need to make sure your terminal or console window is set to your project's root directory.\r\n\r\n### PowerShell ISE\r\n\r\nIf you import the module in the PowerShell ISE, it will add a menu shortcut under `Add-Ons`.\r\n\r\n![add-on menu","target":"images/ise-update.png","line":677},{"title":"ISE update status","target":"images/update-psprojectstatus-ise.png","line":696,"embedded":true},{"title":"VSCode additional command","target":"images/code-update.png","line":704,"embedded":true},{"title":"VSCode update status","target":"images/update-psprojectstatus.png","line":708,"embedded":true},{"title":"schema file","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jdhitsolutions/PSProjectStatus/main/psproject.schema.json","line":714},{"title":"Discussions","target":"https://github.com/jdhitsolutions/PSProjectStatus/discussions","line":732},{"title":"Icons8","target":"https://icons8.com","line":734}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
